nOptions:\n- Fold (-1): Gives up equity unnecessarily. You're likely ahead of bluffs or weaker pairs.\n- Check (0): Not valid — opponent has already raised to 800; you must match or fold/raise.\n- Call (0 action means call here due to context): effectively paying 400 more to see turn card.\n- Raise to 800 or more: aggressive move, but risky — opponent has shown strength. Over-raising could price yourself into a bad spot if behind.\n- All-in (-2): Possible (~19.5k left), but overkill unless you're committed. Might scare off worse hands, but also gets called by better ones.\n\nBest move: **Call 800** (i.e., invest 400 more to match the bet). This allows you to realize your equity, potentially improve (e.g., pairing 10 for two pair, or hitting King/Jack for straight draw later), and avoid overcommitting.\n\nReason:  \nYou have a strong hand with good showdown value and a strong kicker. The opponent’s aggression suggests some strength, but their initial check on the flop after you bet suggests they weren’t thrilled about their hand. Their raise may represent a draw, second pair, or marginal top pair. Calling maintains pot control and lets you evaluate on the turn. Going all-in or folding now would be premature.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
